Z||000001||Old Lar||07-25-2001||06:51 PM||||I paid $2100 for a 3.1 from ATK, then didn't get the serial# from the block (in a timely manner),  I sent my bad 2.8 long block back for a $75 refund.  But since I didn't have the serial # no money was forth coming.<P>The 3.1 had a bad cam, no serial # registered, no warrenty.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Leadfoot||07-25-2001||07:05 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Old Lar:<BR><B>I paid $2100 for a 3.1 from ATK, then didn't get the serial# from the block </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah! I know what you mean about the serial #.  They supposedly glued mine to the block but it wasn't where it was supposed to be.  Good thing the warrant card had the number on it.  Still, I think $1500 for a rebuilt block with a 3 year warranty isn't too bad.  The engine is running strong (knock on wood) but I still am fuming about my decision.  I really wish I new about this forum sooner!<P>||||reg||1
